      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 75-year-old man was diagnosed with sigmoid colon cancer with multiple liver metastases at our hospital in May 2010. He underwent mFOLFOX6 and panitumumab chemotherapy for 6 months. He then underwent sigmoidectomy, lymphadenectomy D3, partial resection of 2 parts of S6, and cholecystectomy in January 2011. However, he underwent partial resection of the liver an additional 4 times in the 5 years followingthe primary operation. Despite multiple liver metastases, he is alive 5 years after the primary operation, havingsurvived 5 hepatectomies for multiple resectable liver metastases."},
